+//
+// The repacked pair is exactly D.w wide, so it fits inside D — and D is
+// disjoint from every upper tile's footprint by construction, so the shared
+// input becomes a globally disjoint mosaic and the cross-tile collision is
+// dissolved rather than merely relabelled. The runtime then splits D at
